+/*
+ * A property read on a string primitive, such as `"abc".charCodeAt`. The
+ * receiver has no shape for the per-site cache to key on. A string's own
+ * properties are `length` and its indices, both excluded here; this answers
+ * the case of an own plain data slot of String.prototype.
+ *
+ * The runtime keeps one hint per atom bucket: the slot index the atom had last
+ * time, re-proved against the prototype's current shape on every use, so a
+ * stale hint or another realm's prototype can only miss.
